### 4. Data Leakage Prevention (Sklearn Pipeline)

> *"I used Scikit-Learn Pipelines to encapsulate transformers. The mean/std used for scaling is derived strictly from training data."*

#### [MODIFY] [ml.py](file:///c:/Users/laxmi/EDA%20automation/analysis/ml.py)
- Refactor `train_quick_model()` to use `sklearn.pipeline.Pipeline`:
  - Wrap `StandardScaler` + model into a Pipeline
  - Ensure `fit()` is only called on training split
  - Remove the current manual `scaler.fit_transform(X)` before split (this is the leakage!)
  - Add pipeline export capability (for the "Code Generation" feature)

> [!WARNING]
> **Current code has actual data leakage!** Line 118 in `ml.py` does `scaler.fit_transform(X)` on the entire dataset before `train_test_split`. This means test set statistics leak into training. The fix wraps everything in a Pipeline that fits only on training data.

